---
description: Ask the user to confirm before creating any git commit
alwaysApply: true
---

# Confirm before commit

Do not create a git commit until the user has confirmed that exact commit.

State the files and the proposed message, then wait. A later commit needs its own confirmation. When the user names the commits and tells you to create them, that message confirms only those commits.

Do not set author or committer values, and do not change git config. Run `git commit` with the message only, so git uses the default user.
